From bd7cbbecd35d0073926163eeee812401c3d69aae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuuzulight <yuuzulight@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:34:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Child frames work for CDP clients: contexts, evaluation,
 describeNode

A client could list a child frame but not look into it: the frame had no
execution context, Runtime commands always ran in the page's realm, and
DOM.describeNode never said which frame owned an element. Playwright and
Puppeteer need all three to read or act inside an iframe.

- announce a default execution context (and the client's isolated worlds)
  when a child frame appears
- aim Runtime and DOM commands at the frame that holds the object, or whose
  context, the command names; object ids minted in a frame carry that frame
- describeNode reports frameId on <html> and on <iframe>/<frame>, and
  describes nodes of a child frame from the object itself
- setFileInputFiles resolves an object id in whatever frame holds it
- a frameset document becomes a body of iframes, so its frames load
- a frame realm gets its object registry on first use, however it was made
